## API Conventions

### Response Envelope

All endpoints return a standard envelope:

```json
{
  "data": { ... },
  "error": null
}
```

On error:

```json
{
  "data": null,
  "error": "Descriptive message"
}
```

<% if (backendFramework === 'fastapi-sqlalchemy') { -%>
FastAPI native errors use `{"detail": "message"}` format.
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'django') { -%>
DRF validation errors use `{"field_name": ["error message"]}` format by default — wrap in the envelope.
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'express') { -%>
Express error middleware should catch and wrap all errors into the envelope format.
<% } else if (backendFramework === 'nestjs') { -%>
NestJS exception filters should catch and wrap all errors into the envelope format.
<% } -%>

### HTTP Status Codes

| Code | Usage |
|---|---|
| 200 | Success (GET, PUT, PATCH) |
| 201 | Created (POST) |
| 204 | No content (DELETE) |
| 400 | Validation error / bad request |
| 401 | Unauthenticated |
| 403 | Forbidden (insufficient permissions) |
| 404 | Resource not found |
| 409 | Conflict (duplicate, state violation) |
| 422 | Validation failure |
| 500 | Internal error (never expose stack traces) |

### Route Prefix

All API routes use the `/api/v1` prefix.

